            <ArticleTitle>[The treatment of organic pain of the peripheral nervous system using clomipramine. 30 cases (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>843-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clomipramine used alone is an affective analgesic against organic pain due to a lesion of the peripheral nervous system, in particular post-herpetic pain. The quality of the result is related to the dose, and hence to tolerance. Fluohydrocortisone is the most powerful drug against orthostatic hypotension, the chief cause of limitation of treatment. No complications were seen, even in very elderly patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
